---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#FAFAFA] flex flex-col">

    <!-- Navigation -->
    <nav id="navbar" class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 bg-[#FAFAFA] px-8 py-6 flex justify-between items-center transition-shadow duration-300">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full flex justify-between items-center">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2 group">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-[#2563EB] rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center group-hover:bg-[#F97316] transition-colors duration-300">
            <span class="font-mono text-white text-sm font-bold">SR</span>
          </div>
          <span class="font-mono text-[#1A1A2E] text-sm font-medium hidden md:block">sroberts.dev</span>
        </a>
        <div class="flex gap-8 text-sm font-medium text-[#6B7280]">
          <a href="/about" class="hover:text-[#1A1A2E] transition-colors">About</a>
          <a href="/projects" class="text-[#1A1A2E]">Projects</a>
          <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-[#1A1A2E] transition-colors">Blog</a>
          <a href="/#contact" class="hover:text-[#1A1A2E] transition-colors">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="flex-grow">

      <!-- Back link + header -->
      <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8 pt-40 pb-12">
        <a href="/projects/ctf-challenges" class="font-mono text-[#F97316] text-sm tracking-wider hover:underline">← Back to CTF Challenges</a>
        <p class="font-mono text-[#F97316] text-sm mt-6 mb-2 tracking-wider">Beginner</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-6 leading-tight">
          The Vault
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-[#6B7280] leading-relaxed">
          A small company's internal server has been left exposed. Find a
          way in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Narrative -->
      <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8 pb-16 space-y-6 text-[#6B7280] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          No solution steps here - the brief should point you in the right direction!
          What follows is the general shape of the challenge, 
          although this one serves as a proof off concept for more intersting challenges to come, 
          I have incorporated real tools, and a realistic, although simplified attack chain.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] pt-6">The scenario</h2>
        <p>
          A recon-to-root chain: start with nothing but a target, and work
          your way from an initial scan through to a sturdy foothold on the
          system. Each stage only opens up once the previous one's actually
          been done correctly.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] pt-6">Tools involved</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-[#E5E7EB]">
            <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-1 font-mono text-sm">nmap</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">Network scanning - finding what's actually open on the target</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-[#E5E7EB]">
            <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-1 font-mono text-sm">ftp</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">A structured protocol for file transfer - Uploads & Downloads</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-[#E5E7EB]">
            <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-1 font-mono text-sm">curl</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">The tool for pulling web content directly - no browser needed</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-[#E5E7EB]">
            <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-1 font-mono text-sm">john the ripper</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">Password cracking - turning a hash into something usable</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-[#E5E7EB]">
            <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-1 font-mono text-sm">netcat (nc)</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">A raw, protocol-agnostic connection - no protocol niceties</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A2E] pt-6">Small tip</h2>
        <p>
          Two ports come up early in this one. They're not interchangeable -
          one's a proper file-transfer service, the other's a raw, unlabelled
          listener. Which tool you reach for depends entirely on which kind
          of port you're dealing with.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-white border border-[#E5E7EB] rounded-xl p-6 mt-8">
          <p class="text-sm text-[#6B7280]">
            Ready to try it? Open the terminal, type <code class="bg-[#F3F4F6] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">ctf</code>,
            then <code class="bg-[#F3F4F6] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">1</code> or
            <code class="bg-[#F3F4F6] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">the-vault</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="bg-[#1A1A2E] border-t border-white/10 py-6">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-8 flex justify-between items-center">
        <span class="font-mono text-[#6B7280] text-sm">© 2026 Scott Roberts</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-[#6B7280] text-sm">sroberts.dev</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <script>
    const navbar = document.getElementById('navbar');
    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      if (window.scrollY > 10) {
        navbar?.classList.add('shadow-md');
      } else {
        navbar?.classList.remove('shadow-md');
      }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
